<BaseLayout title="Methodology | GearPilot AI" description="The transparent standing desk eligibility and scoring methodology used by GearPilot AI." canonicalPath="/methodology/">
  <h1>How we compare standing desks</h1>
  <p>First, we filter to the US market and require a verified exact product/configuration, a fresh known total price, fresh in-stock availability, workspace dimensions, height range, lift capacity, and any required electric adjustment. Publication also requires source-backed specifications, independent product editorial approval, and configuration-applicable warranty and return evidence. Unknown fields never pass a hard requirement.</p>
  <p>Eligible products receive a deterministic comparison score. Value weights price most heavily; quality weights capacity and warranty; workspace fit weights desktop size and height range. The calculation uses documented price, dimensions, capacity, warranty, and evidence status—never affiliate commission rates.</p>
  <p>Product discovery and evidence collection are not endorsements. A research candidate is kept separate from verified products. A commercial observation requires a named collector and independent reviewer; approving that observation does not by itself verify or publish a product, create an offer, or approve an affiliate relationship. Product, offer, and affiliate approval are separate decisions.</p>
  <p>A verified record includes source provenance for the exact product and its documented specifications. Price and mandatory-shipping observations expire after seven days and in-stock observations after three days; stale, unreviewed, conflicting, or unknown offers are excluded rather than guessed. Any displayed real price would be an observation timestamped in UTC, not a claim of live pricing. The public finder currently uses clearly labeled synthetic demo data, never a real listing, price, review, or hands-on test.</p>
  <p>Scores compare the eligible catalog entries for the selected criteria. They are not star ratings or claims of hands-on testing.</p>
</BaseLayout>
